171
00:14:06,126 --> 00:14:08,740
that's called Attention is All You Need,

172
00:14:09,742 --> 00:14:17,860
that introduced a new architecture that relied on a paradigm that proved to be very scalable.

173
00:14:18,990 --> 00:14:21,668
By scalable, I mean if you give

174
00:14:22,382 --> 00:14:24,836
your model more data, more compute,

175
00:14:25,518 --> 00:14:26,660
and more parameters,

176
00:14:27,534 --> 00:14:29,956
you're actually able to see performance gains

177
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:34,276
that are far greater compared to what you used to see before.

178
00:14:35,438 --> 00:14:40,292
And it's something that we're going to see today. So this architecture is called the transformer.

179
00:14:41,614 --> 00:14:44,452
And on the right, you have an illustration of

180
00:14:45,390 --> 00:14:49,188
how it's illustrated in the original paper. We're going to see how it works.

181
00:14:50,606 --> 00:14:51,456
And from there,

182
00:14:52,398 --> 00:14:56,356
people have taken this architecture and just scaled

183
00:14:57,262 --> 00:15:04,132
it from a model size perspective, but also from the number of tokens it's been trained on.

184
00:15:04,896 --> 00:15:09,956
And this is how modern day LLMs have come into the picture.

185
00:15:10,542 --> 00:15:13,060
LLMs that actually know, I mean, that

186
00:15:13,774 --> 00:15:17,092
actually generate text pretty well, that generate code pretty well.

